tasks.description:
Implement the deferred Zed integration baseline. Evidence: repo search found no `setup zed` command and no Zed setup docs/config, while `BACKLOG.md:P3-6` defines the intended MCP-first approach. Acceptance: users can configure Agent Plan for Zed via a documented/setup path that does not implicitly initialize `.planner/`.

---
**Completion summary:**
Completed Zed MCP setup documentation. No Zed extension was built, per user request.

Deliverables:
- docs/setup-zed.md — full setup guide for adding Agent Plan as a custom/local context server in Zed:
  - install `agent-plan` globally;
  - add the `agent-plan` context server to Zed settings (npx agent-plan mcp);
  - verify active status in Settings → AI → MCP Servers;
  - run `planner-init` per project;
  - planner root resolution and AGENT_PLAN_ROOT override;
  - example prompts for the Zed Agent Panel;
  - custom agent profile to force planner-only tooling;
  - task guard model note (Zed lacks PreToolUse hook);
  - references to Claude Code/Codex docs and public schema.
- README.md — added docs/setup-zed.md to the Documentation list.
- docs/setup-claude-code.md — added Zed setup cross-reference.
- docs/setup-codex.md — added Zed setup cross-reference.

Validation:
- pnpm check (root typecheck) passes.
- No code changes beyond Markdown and README edits.
